FINDINGS (audit record -- run 2026-08-31):
  1. The UNCOMMITTED route2_v2 cache L2dc_v2.pkl FAILS the hard anchors when
     actually run: Newton != 8pi/(1-K_B/2) (at any J_Y; verified symbolically
     in J_Y), alpha_1 = +5.75 at K_B=1/5 (vs required -4K_B = -0.8; J_Y->oo
     limit = +8, a K_B-INDEPENDENT pure number), alpha_3 = 2*alpha_1 != 0.
     The ground-note claim that route2_v2 'passes alpha_1=-4K_B at test
     points' does NOT reproduce on this cache.  Its alpha_2 values are NOT
     quotable.  T1/T2 must rebuild/repair before any SOLVE-A/B verdict.
  2. Diagnostic: alpha_2(cache) ~ -1/(K2 Q0^2) diverges in the PPN hierarchy
     Q0/k_x -> 0: the K2=F_QQ channel's STATIC stiffness is Q0^2-weighted
     (certified in t3x_structural_deltaQ_projection.py [C.2]), so it cannot
     regulate the c123=0 FJ pole at solar wavenumbers -- the pole must be
     regulated by the scalar KINETIC sector (Route 3's eps_eff), not by the
     mass term.  Any solve that regulates via K2 Q0^2 is outside the PPN
     regime (this run's kx=1, Q0=2/5 point included).
  3. The K2-slope of alpha_2 is +0.3..+1.6 = O(1) at all points -- order-of-
     magnitude consistent with the independent Green-function projection
     |Pi_K| = r^2/(2-K_B) F_QQ ~ 0.14..0.7 F_QQ (t3x_greenfunction_PiK.py),
     but NOT quotable as a coefficient given finding 1.
